# RTEC Report layout (SETUP Form 002)

Source of truth: `Form 002 - RTEC Report.docx` — SETUP Guidelines (Revision 3.0) Annex A-2.
Do not import Form 001 checkbox grids onto the official document.

## Document title

`SETUP Form 002 - RTEC Report`

Mixed case. Do **not** force uppercase via CSS. Black text only (no DOST-blue bars on print/preview document).

## Page

- A4 portrait. Margins: **1 in (25.4 mm)** all sides.
- Body: Arial ~11pt.
- `@page rtec-report-sheet` footer:

`SETUP Guidelines (Revision 3.0) Annex A-2: SETUP Form 002 - RTEC Report Page ` + `counter(page)` / `counter(pages)`

## Structure (exact Word order)

1. Title
2. Cover: Project Title / Proponent / Contact Person
3. Project Cost: Proponent | DOST-SETUP | DOST-LGIA | Total
4. **I.** Brief description → a. Company profile (identity lines only) → b. Objectives → c. Expected Outputs / Impact/s
5. **II.** Compliance table — **14 Word rows** × Requirements | Complied | Not Complied (**no N/A column** on print)
6. **III.** Highlights → a Management; b Technical (process flow, material balance, existing equipment, constraint table, Proposed Plant Lay-out, cost table + Total, fabricators); c–f Marketing / Financial ratio narrative / Waste / Risk
7. **IV.** Recommendation + signatures: Evaluated by → Chairperson → Member ×3 → Reviewed and endorsed by / Noted by → RPMO | Regional Director

Evaluation date stays in the staff editor only (not on Word).

## Staff editor (Word field map)

[`RtecReportEditor`](src/app/components/RtecReportEditor.tsx) follows the same Word section order. Prefill from `proposalSnapshot` + RTEC-native fields. Edits stay on the **RTEC draft** (do not write back to Form 001).

| Editor block | Fields |
|---|---|
| Cover | `projectTitle`, `proponentName`, `contactPerson`; `projectCostProponent` / `Setup` / `Lgia` / `Total` |
| I.a | `firmName`, `firmAddress`, `contactPerson`, `contactNumber` |
| I.b–c | `generalObjective`, `specificObjectives`, `expectedOutputBullets` |
| II | Official 14 rows (`RTEC_OFFICIAL_COMPLIANCE_ITEMS`) + portal extras (ECC/FDA/supplier) off-print |
| III.a | `skillsExpertise`, `compensation` |
| III.b | `productionProcess`, `materialBalance`, `equipmentNarrative`, `constraintRows`, plant layout (read-only attachment), `interventionCostTable`, `fabricatorRows` |
| III.c–f | marketing fields, `ratioNarrative`, `wasteManagement`, `riskRows` |
| IV | `recommendation`, signatures (+ editor-only evaluation date) |

Wizard steps: `compliance` → II; `evaluation` → III; `recommendation` → IV; Edit report (`all`) → Cover + I–IV.

`syncRtecFromProjectProposal` uses pick-if-blank for Form 002 editable snapshot fields so staff edits are not wiped.

## Prefill sources (module → editor field)

Primary path: Form 001 (`getProjectProposalForm`) → `proposalSnapshot` / RTEC-native fields. Form 001 is already fed by TNA1, published TNA2, applicant header, and LOI commitment amounts. `enrichRtecSnapshotFromPriorModules` fills **blank** Form 002 narrative gaps from related Form 001 / TNA1 fields after draft build and after Sync pick-if-blank. Edits stay on the RTEC draft (no write-back to Form 001).

| Editor block | Prefill source |
|---|---|
| Cover identity | Form 001 `projectTitle` / `proponentName` / `contactPerson` (← TNA1 / applicant) |
| Cover costs | Form 001 `projectCost`, `amountRequested`, Σ `budgetItems.lgiaShare` → RTEC `projectCost*` |
| I.a Company profile | Form 001 `firmName`, `firmAddress`, `contactPerson`, `contactNumber` |
| I.b–c Objectives / outputs | Form 001 objectives + `expectedOutputBullets` (← TNA2 outcomes / `expectedOutcome`) |
| II Compliance | Suggest from LOI, TNA1/2 submitted/published, Form 001, requirement uploads; Sync pick-if-blank |
| III.a Management | Form 001 `skillsExpertise` / `compensation`; if blank → light seed from proponent + `compensationTable` |
| III.b Process / material / cost table | Form 001 (process ← TNA2 summary or TNA1 `processFlow`); cost table ← TNA2 recommended equipment |
| III.b Existing equipment | Form 001 `equipmentNarrative`; if blank → line list from `equipmentTable` (TNA1) |
| III.b Constraints / fabricators / plant | RTEC `constraintRows` (Form 001 intervention\* or TNA2 gaps); `fabricatorRows`; `attachmentRefs` (+ TNA plant layout) |
| III.c Marketing | Form 001 marketing fields; if blank → `marketSituation` from `distributionChannel`, problems from `competitors`; strategies ← TNA1 plans |
| III.d Financial | RTEC `ratioNarrative` ← Form 001 `financialAnalysis` when present (no invented ratio text) |
| III.e Waste | Form 001 `wasteManagement`; if blank → `wasteKinds` + `wasteDisposalMethods` or TNA1 `wasteManagement` |
| III.f Risk | Form 001 `riskRows` (template defaults on Form 001 draft) |
| IV Recommendation | Draft seed from published TNA2 findings + interventions (Sync preserves staff text) |
| IV Signatures | Regional Director default; others staff-entered |

## Compliance split

- Staff editor: official 14 Word labels + Additional portal checks (3 extras) with N/A allowed.
- Official document: `toOfficialComplianceItems()` → 14 Word rows. Status `na` leaves both tick cells empty.
- Financial row Micro 1yr / SME 3yr wording is Word SoT and the only portal surface for that rule.

## Preview vs print (100% fidelity)

- Preview **mounts** `RtecReportDocument` — same markup as print.
- Print re-renders via `createRoot` (`printRtecReportPdf`). Do **not** clone `#rtec-report-preview`.
- Print root uses class `rtec-form-document` so preview CSS applies.
- No logo / Republic header / Application ID on the official document.
- Staff **Edit report ↔ Preview report** toggle on Preview & PDF (`ConductOfRTEC` `editMode`).

## Print path

In-page `window.print()` to `#rtec-report-print-root` + `body.rtec-report-printing`. Do not use popup `document.write`.

